zard identification"},{"text":"Failure modes"},{"text":"Consequence assessment"},{"text":"Probability concepts"},{"text":"Risk matrices"},{"text":"Risk reduction"},{"text":"Risk-informed decision-making"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A useful framework:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Hazard","Potential Failure Mode","Likelihood","Consequences","Risk","Risk Reduction","Residual Risk"]},{"type":"h","text":"Potential Failure Mode Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to ask:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What can fail?"},{"text":"How can it fail?"},{"text":"What evidence would indicate the failure?"},{"text":"What could cause the failure?"},{"text":"What would happen downstream?"},{"text":"What monitoring could detect it?"},{"text":"What intervention could reduce the risk?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emergency Action Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"A Dam Safety Engineer should understand Emergency Action Plans (EAPs)."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Emergency classification"},{"text":"Warning systems"},{"text":"Notification chains"},{"text":"Downstream inundation"},{"text":"Emergency communication"},{"text":"Evacuation coordination"},{"text":"Emergency access"},{"text":"Incident command"},{"text":"Post-event assessment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Conceptually:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Dam Abnormality","Detection","Assessment","Emergency Classification","Notification","Warning","Emergency Response","Recovery"]},{"type":"p","text":"Exact emergency procedures are facility-specific and must follow approved plans."},{"type":"h","text":"Dam-Break & Inundation Modelling"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Dam-break scenarios"},{"text":"Breach formation"},{"text":"Flood-wave propagation"},{"text":"Downstream inundation"},{"text":"Travel time"},{"text":"Depth"},{"text":"Velocity"},{"text":"Hazard mapping"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful tools/concepts:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HEC-RAS"},{"text